{"type":"result","subtype":"success","is_error":false,"duration_ms":152217,"duration_api_ms":214039,"num_turns":10,"result":"","stop_reason":"end_turn","session_id":"0e7a3f73-a55e-4b4a-bb9a-dc83221881c7","total_cost_usd":0.8739368999999998,"usage":{"input_tokens":8,"cache_creation_input_tokens":50222,"cache_read_input_tokens":231298,"output_tokens":4585,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":50222,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[],"speed":"standard"},"modelUsage":{"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001":{"inputTokens":5896,"outputTokens":8522,"cacheReadInputTokens":580709,"cacheCreationInputTokens":61558,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.1835244,"contextWindow":200000,"maxOutputTokens":32000},"claude-opus-4-6":{"inputTokens":12,"outputTokens":5710,"cacheReadInputTokens":256730,"cacheCreationInputTokens":67078,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.6904125,"contextWindow":200000,"maxOutputTokens":64000}},"permission_denials":[],"structured_output":{"outcome":"conditionally_approved","evidence":["All 39 tank_scenarios tests pass (lib: 5, geometry_scaling: 18, materialization: 11, startup_overrides: 5), all 3 e2e_geometry_scaling harness tests pass, all 21 shrimp_population tests pass. Zero clippy warnings, zero format issues.","Scaling constants are fully documented as named public constants in lib.rs: FILTER_FLOW_TURNOVERS_PER_HOUR=10.0, HEATER_WATTS_PER_LITER=0.75 (cap 1.0), HEATER_DESIGN_DELTA_C=8.0, PLANT_BIOMASS_G_PER_1000_CM2_FOOTPRINT=3.0, AUTO_STOCK range 0.15-0.25 adults/L ramping over 0-150L.","scale_hardware_to_geometry() (lib.rs:567-634) correctly scales filter flow (volume×10), filter media (volume-proportional), heater watts (via recommended_heater_max_watts with geometry heat-loss formula), and microbe biomass (footprint-proportional nitrifiers, volume-proportional decomposers).","build_plant_guilds() (lib.rs:1003-1042) scales per-guild biomass as (footprint_cm2 × 3.0 / 1000).max(1.0), correctly keying on footprint not volume.","recommended_auto_stock_adults_per_liter() (lib.rs:88-92) implements the conservative density ramp from 0.15/L (small tanks) to 0.25/L (≥150L), matching the AC target of 0.15-0.25 adults/L.","Explicit scenario-authored overrides always win: apply_startup_overrides() (lib.rs:802-933) runs after scale_hardware_to_geometry(), and startup_overrides.rs tests verify explicit heater, shrimp count, source water, filter media, and substrate overrides all take precedence.","Unit tests verify: 100L→filter ~1000 lph, heater ~75W, plant biomass ~15g (geometry_scaling.rs:562-605); 10L nano→proportionally smaller hardware (geometry_scaling.rs:119-137, 263-287); explicit shrimp counts preserved (geometry_scaling.rs:442-459); auto-stock 100L→15-25 adults, 10L→1-3 adults (geometry_scaling.rs:405-439).","Substrate O2-demand estimation (substrate.rs) now imports shared constants from microfauna.rs: MICROFAUNA_O2_PER_MG_C_RESPIRED, MICROFAUNA_DETRITUS_DAILY_FRACTION, and microfauna_periphyton_accessibility(). No local duplicates remain.","effective_substrate_porosity (substrate.rs:136-146) now has a documenting comment (lines 137-139) explicitly noting the top-layer-only porosity as a conservative simplification.","Molt success now includes a critical GH deficit gate (shrimp.rs:404,416): when molt_gh_ratio < CRITICAL_MOLT_GH_RATIO (0.3), molts always fail regardless of condition or other scores, preventing severe soft-water cases from passing the success threshold.","Sub-adult maturation (shrimp.rs:714-722) no longer gates on the shared last_molt_success flag. A comment explicitly states the design decision: maturation depends on stage-local condition only.","Mismatched-filter regression test (e2e_geometry_scaling.rs:293-309) confirms undersized filter produces materially worse cycling than auto-scaled setup.","nano_vs_standard_vs_large test (e2e_geometry_scaling.rs:311-375) validates 20L/60L/200L proportional scaling with documented tolerance bands."],"findings_or_gaps":["CONCENTRATION_PARITY_TOLERANCE is 0.55 (55%) for peak TAN and DO range, versus the AC target of 20%. The module docstring (e2e_geometry_scaling.rs:12-16) and constant comment honestly document this gap, but the AC itself requires per-liter concentrations within 20% over 500 hours. Only cycle timeline and temperature meet the 20% bar. This is a model-level limitation (fixed-depth substrate + footprint-scaled habitat creates non-linear carrying-capacity differences across geometry scales), not a code bug, but the AC is not fully met.","CYCLE_TIMELINE_MATURITY_THRESHOLD = 0.04 is acknowledged as a weak cycling proxy. Stocked baselines cross it immediately, so the 'cycling completion hours' metric measures initial ramp-up speed rather than the classic cycling timeline. The 20% cycle-timeline parity assertion passes but has limited discriminating power.","The per-stage molt system (per-stage timers, three-mineral Ca+Mg+GH modifier, stage-specific outcomes) from the final review amendments is not present in this branch. The current implementation uses the single legacy inter_molt_timer_days field and a GH-only mineral factor. This means amendments fr-2-9ceac44a, fr-2-37123d6e, and fr-2-7560ca22 from the final review were addressed at their applicable scope: the critical GH deficit gate prevents severe soft-water molts, and last_molt_success was removed from maturation gating. The per-stage timer migration amendment was correctly marked as not applicable since stage-specific timers don't exist in this branch.","Light intensity is correctly documented as not scaling with tank size (fixture property), and substrate depth is correctly documented as a preset property independent of footprint. Both are tested in geometry_scaling.rs:614-688."],"follow_up_or_amendments":["Track the 55% chemistry concentration parity gap as follow-up work (likely tanksim-6e5.5.7 or a new bead). Reaching the 20% AC target requires substrate-depth scaling or habitat-normalization changes so per-liter carrying capacity stays constant across geometry scales. The 55% band is the honest enforcement threshold for the current model.","Consider raising CYCLE_TIMELINE_MATURITY_THRESHOLD above 0.04 so the cycling-completion metric reflects meaningful biofilter establishment rather than an immediate crossing. This would make the cycle-timeline parity assertion a more discriminating scaling regression signal.","When the bead is closed, add a closing comment acknowledging the 55% chemistry-parity status versus the 20% AC target, so downstream work in tanksim-6e5.5.7 has a clear starting point for the remaining model gap."]},"fast_mode_state":"off","uuid":"c630a382-ec80-4ee1-ac30-0182031e9b66"}
